.TH DRIVHUS-IOT 1 "September 2026" "drivhus-iot" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
drivhus-iot \- greenhouse IoT MQTT subscriber
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B drivhus-iot
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B drivhus-iot
subscribes to greenhouse MQTT topics, processes sensor telemetry and
PlantCV analysis messages, and republishes the processed data for
storage by Telegraf and PostgreSQL.
.PP
The program normally runs as a systemd service.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/drivhus-subscriber/config.json
JSON configuration file.
.TP
.I /opt/drivhus-subscriber/drivhus-iot
Installed executable.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/drivhus-iot.service
systemd service definition.
.SH SERVICE COMMANDS
Start the service:
.PP
.nf
sudo systemctl start drivhus-iot
.fi
.PP
Stop the service:
.PP
.nf
sudo systemctl stop drivhus-iot
.fi
.PP
Check its status:
.PP
.nf
sudo systemctl status drivhus-iot
.fi
.PP
View live logs:
.PP
.nf
journalctl -u drivhus-iot -f
.fi
.SH MQTT TOPICS
.TP
.I sensors/drivhusServer/raw
Incoming sensor telemetry.
.TP
.I plants/drivhusServer/plant_analysis
Incoming PlantCV analysis results.
.TP
.I drivhusData/drivhusServer/telemetry
Processed telemetry.
.TP
.I drivhusData/drivhusServer/plant_analysis
Processed PlantCV results.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Greenhouse IoT project